{"name":"Sea Hunter","hex":"#245878","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sea","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Semai."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large body of salt water.","The ocean; the continuous body of salt water covering a majority of the Earth's surface."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sea"},{"term":"hunter","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who hunts game for sport or for food; a huntsman or huntswoman.","A dog used in hunting; a hunting dog."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hunter"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sea Hunter","blocks":[{"text":"Sea Hunter is an autonomous unmanned surface vehicle (USV) launched in 2016 as part of the DARPA Anti-Submarine Warfare Continuous Trail Unmanned Vessel (ACTUV) program. The ship was christened 7 April 2016 in Portland, Oregon. It was designed and built by Leidos, with manufacturing subcontracted to Christensen Shipyards. The vessel continues the line of experimental \"Sea\" ships, including Sea Shadow, Sea Fighter, Sea Jet, and Sea Slice. Sea Hunter is classified as a Class III USV and designated the Medium Displacement Unmanned Surface Vehicle (MDUSV)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/USV_Sea_Hunter_-_RIMPAC_2022_Fleet_Sails_in_Formation.jpg/330px-USV_Sea_Hunter_-_RIMPAC_2022_Fleet_Sails_in_Formation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea_Hunter","wikidata":"Q23806451"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea","wikidata":"Q165"},{"title":"Hunting","blocks":[{"text":"Hunting is the human practice of seeking, pursuing, capturing, and/or killing wildlife or feral animals. The most common reasons for humans to hunt are to obtain the animal's body to consume their meat and useful animal products, for recreation/taxidermy, although it may also be done for other purposes such as removing predators dangerous to humans or domestic animals, to eliminate pests and nuisance animals that damage crops/livestock/poultry or spread diseases, for trade/tourism, or for ecological conservation against overpopulation and invasive species."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Paul_Childerley_driven_hunt_Finland_04.png/330px-Paul_Childerley_driven_hunt_Finland_04.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hunting","wikidata":"Q36963"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Sea_Hunter_gets_underway_on_the_Willamette_River_following_a_christening_ceremony_in_Portland%2C_Ore._%2825702146834%29.jpg/500px-Sea_Hunter_gets_underway_on_the_Willamette_River_following_a_christening_ceremony_in_Portland%2C_Ore._%2825702146834%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Sea_Hunter_gets_underway_on_the_Willamette_River_following_a_christening_ceremony_in_Portland%2C_Ore._%2825702146834%29.jpg/1280px-Sea_Hunter_gets_underway_on_the_Willamette_River_following_a_christening_ceremony_in_Portland%2C_Ore._%2825702146834%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Sea_Hunter_gets_underway_on_the_Willamette_River_follo